  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 148 PM CDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nTuesday through Sunday:\n\nModels continue to show a slowing trend with the increasing\nmoisture and shortwave this week. The deeper moisture and rain\nchances may hold off until at least late Tuesday night or \nWednesday per the bulk of 12Z guidance, with some solutions\nholding off until nearly Thursday. Eventually, precipitable \nwater values of 1.5-2.0\" are expected to push through the \nforecast area along and ahead of the trough passage, bringing \nwidespread rain chances to southern Wisconsin. Still not seeing\nmuch instability and mid-level lapse rates are expected to be \non the lower end, so kept just a slight chance for thunder. High\ntemps will remain a bit above normal through Wednesday, with \nsoutherly winds expected ahead of the approaching trough. \n\nThe trough should clear the area by Thursday night, with strong\nhigh pressure moving in for Friday into the weekend. Dry weather\nis likely Friday and Saturday, with a shortwave possibly \nbringing a few showers to the area on Sunday. Somewhat cooler \nconditions are expected Fri-Sun under the high. \n\nDDV",
